From 97890f0e74f718528b1ba67aec9aeecc34df2ec4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:10:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 27/27] proxy/pf: spread over endpoints listening on different
 ports

A named targetPort can resolve to different ports on different endpoints
(e.g. during a rollout that changes the container port). An rdr rule
redirects to one port, so only the largest group of endpoints sharing a
port got traffic and the others none. Keep every port group and, when a
service has more than one, redirect with filter rules (pass in quick ...
rdr-to, FreeBSD 15): one per group, each but the last with a probability
matching its share of the endpoints, so connections spread as over one
pool. loadBalancerSourceRanges then blocks other sources ahead of them.
Hairpin, NodePort SNAT, host rules and UDP state cleanup cover every
group. Services whose endpoints share a port keep the same rules.

Fixes the e2e test "should support named targetPorts that resolve to
different ports on different endpoints".
